---
source: tests/refusal_snapshots_m4.rs
expression: s
---
copying onto something that is already there
  exit 2  refusing: something is already here. ricepilot copies into a name nothing occupies, so that an interrupted earlier attempt is something you can look at rather than something this overwrote (<HOME>/rice/occupied) [R2]

copying a tree into itself
  exit 2  refusing: is inside <HOME>/rice/src, so copying one into the other would never finish (<HOME>/rice/src/inner) [R5]

copying something that is not there
  exit 2  refusing: there is nothing here to copy (<HOME>/rice/nothing) [R5]

copying a tree with a socket in it
  exit 2  refusing: is neither a directory, a regular file nor a symlink. ricepilot will not pretend a copy of a socket or a fifo is the same object; declare it volatile or move it aside (<HOME>/rice/src/app.sock) [R5]

recovering an adopt whose directory was replaced underneath it
  exit 2  refusing: an interrupted adopt left this path as a different directory (inode <n>, not the inode <n> that was confirmed), which is neither the directory that was adopted nor the link it was becoming. something else changed it while ricepilot was not looking, and ricepilot will not guess what (<HOME>/.config/hypr) [R4]
